# Copy this file to .dev.vars for LOCAL testing with `wrangler dev`.
# Never commit real values. In production the SECRET values below (not the
# non-secret [vars] ones) are set with `wrangler secret put <NAME>` instead.
#
# (If you previously filled in a .env file for the Vercel version, copy the
# same values over — the names are identical.)

# --- Anthropic ---
# From console.anthropic.com. This key calls the Coach.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Postmark ---
# Server API Token, found in Postmark: your Server > API Tokens.
# Used to SEND the report back (separate from the inbound webhook, which
# doesn't need a token since Postmark calls YOU).
POSTMARK_SERVER_TOKEN=

# --- Supabase ---
# Project URL and SERVICE ROLE key (not the public anon key — this function
# runs server-side and needs full read/write access to your tables).
# Found in Supabase: Project Settings > API.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Note: ANTHROPIC_MODEL, FROM_EMAIL, and REVIEW_DOMAIN are not secrets —
# they live in wrangler.toml under [vars].

# --- Stripe (TEST MODE — see stripe-billing-build-spec.md Part 10) ---
# wrangler.toml's [vars] hold the LIVE price/coupon IDs and the deployed
# Worker's secret is the LIVE key — this section is the local-only test-mode
# mirror of those same five values, so `wrangler dev` never touches real
# money while you're testing.
#
# Toggle the Stripe Dashboard to test mode (top-right) before copying any of
# these. STRIPE_SECRET_KEY: Developers > API keys > Secret key (sk_test_...).
# STRIPE_PRICE_MONTHLY / STRIPE_PRICE_ANNUAL / STRIPE_COUPON_ANNUAL_DISCOUNT:
# the test-mode Product/Coupon you created in Part 1 step 2-3 — if you did
# Part 1 in test mode first as instructed, these already exist; just copy
# their IDs again rather than recreating them.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
STRIPE_PRICE_MONTHLY=
STRIPE_PRICE_ANNUAL=
STRIPE_COUPON_ANNUAL_DISCOUNT=

# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET is DIFFERENT from the Dashboard endpoint's signing
# secret (Part 1 step 5) — that one is for the live endpoint you create only
# after this checklist passes. For local testing, `stripe listen` prints its
# own whsec_... the moment you run it; paste THAT one here instead.
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
